sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / DSP API Server
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant WFC as Workflow Controller<br/>9090/TCP metrics
    participant Pod as Workflow Pod
    participant AE as argoexec<br/>(init + sidecar)
    participant Artifacts as Artifact Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP SSL

    Note over User, DB: Flow 1: Workflow Execution

    User->>K8sAPI: 1. Create Workflow CR<br/>HTTPS/443 | Bearer Token (SA)
    K8sAPI-->>WFC: 2. Informer notification<br/>HTTPS/443 | ServiceAccount token
    WFC->>K8sAPI: 3. Create execution Pod<br/>HTTPS/443 | ServiceAccount token

    Note over Pod, AE: Pod starts with argoexec as init + sidecar

    AE->>Artifacts: 4. Download input artifacts (init)<br/>HTTPS/443 | Access key/IAM
    Artifacts-->>AE: Artifact data

    Note over Pod: User container executes<br/>(argoexec emissary wraps process)

    AE->>K8sAPI: 5. Patch WorkflowTaskResult<br/>HTTPS/443 | ServiceAccount token
    AE->>Artifacts: 6. Upload output artifacts (wait)<br/>HTTPS/443 | Access key/IAM
    Artifacts-->>AE: Upload confirmed

    WFC->>DB: 7. Archive workflow (optional)<br/>TCP/5432 | DB credentials (SSL)
    DB-->>WFC: Archived

    WFC-->>K8sAPI: Update Workflow status
    K8sAPI-->>User: Workflow completed

    Note over User, DB: Flow 2: Webhook Event Submission

    participant GitProv as Git Provider<br/>(GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket)
    participant ArgoSrv as Argo Server<br/>2746/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+

    GitProv->>ArgoSrv: 1. POST webhook event<br/>HTTPS/2746 | HMAC-SHA256 signature
    ArgoSrv->>K8sAPI: 2. Read webhook Secret<br/>HTTPS/443 | ServiceAccount token
    K8sAPI-->>ArgoSrv: Secret data (HMAC key)
    Note over ArgoSrv: Verify HMAC-SHA256 signature
    ArgoSrv->>K8sAPI: 3. Create Workflow CR<br/>HTTPS/443 | Webhook SA token
    K8sAPI-->>ArgoSrv: Workflow created
